<section class="pursue-part career-mccombs" id="mccombs" aria-labelledby="mccombs-heading">
    <div class="career-wrap">
        <h2 class="career-section-title" id="mccombs-heading">McCombs at a Glance</h2>
        <div class="mccombs-grid">
            <ul class="mccombs-stats" aria-label="McCombs rankings, U.S. News &amp; World Report">
                <li><b>#1</b><span>Graduate Information Systems program in the US</span></li>
                <li><b>#4</b><span>Management Information Systems, my major</span></li>
                <li><b>#5</b><span>Marketing, my minor</span></li>
                <li><b>#6</b><span>Undergraduate business school in the US</span></li>
                <li><b>Top 10</b><span>Ten of our BBA programs rank here</span></li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mccombs-text">
                <p>If you want to learn to build technology for people, you go where it’s taught best. My major comes out of the same McCombs department behind the country’s top graduate Information Systems program, and it shows in how the classes are built: less memorizing, more <em>go build the real thing</em>.</p>
                <p>Marketing sits right next door, so the psychology of why people choose what they choose is never far from the code. The rankings got me in the door. The people, the professors who know your name and classmates who push each other, are why I stay.</p>
                <p class="mccombs-source">Rankings: <a href="https://www.usnews.com/best-colleges/university-of-texas-at-austin-3658/overall-rankings" target="_blank" rel="noopener">U.S. News &amp; World Report ↗</a></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pursue-part career-experience" id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
    <div class="career-wrap">
        <h2 class="career-section-title" id="experience-heading">Experience</h2>
        <div class="job-list">
            @foreach (var (when, title, where, points) in jobs)
            {
                <article class="job">
                    <span class="job-when">@when</span>
                    <h3>@title</h3>
                    <p class="job-where">@where</p>
                    <ul>
                        @foreach (var point in points)
                        {
                            <li>@point</li>
                        }
                    </ul>
                </article>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

